# Crime ingest and storage

Scheduled job (cron, Cloud Function, or APScheduler) reads **static/historical** files or a dump—not a live NYPD API. Map rows into the common schema and upsert by `source_id`.

```python
# ❌ BAD
db.add(Incident(lat=row.lat, lng=row.lng))  # duplicates on every run

# ✅ GOOD
stmt = insert(Incident).values(...).on_conflict_do_update(
    index_elements=[Incident.source_id],
    set_={"severity": ..., "timestamp": ..., "geom": ...},
)
```

## PostGIS

Store location as `geography(Point,4326)` (or `geometry` SRID 4326) with a **GIST** index. Keep `severity` numeric and `category` a small enum or closed text set.

```sql
-- ✅ GOOD
geom geography(Point, 4326) NOT NULL,
CREATE INDEX incidents_geom_gix ON incidents USING GIST (geom);
```

## Replay clock

Queries must filter `timestamp` around `sim_now`, not wall-clock now. Expose `sim_now` (config, env, or a small table) so ingest replay and scoring share the same clock.
